            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Carissa bispinosa grows as a shrub or small tree up to {{convert|5|m}} tall. Its fragrant flowers feature a white corolla. The fruit is red when ripe. Its habitat is woodland and forest from {{convert|1080|m|abbr=on}} to {{convert|1630|m|abbr=on}} elevation. Vernacular names for the plant include forest num-num and Y-thorned carissa. Carissa bispinosa is native to an area from Uganda to South Africa."
          }
        ]
      }
